---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Drukhari Beginner's Guide — Warhammer 40k"
  description="New to Drukhari? Learn how they play, which sub-faction to choose, how to paint their dark armor, and exactly what to buy first."
>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="px-6 pt-16 pb-12 border-b border-[#2a2a35]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/factions/" class="text-sm text-[#4a4855] hover:text-[#8a8590] transition-colors mb-6 inline-block">
        ← All Factions
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-6">
        <div class="text-6xl">🗡️</div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-[#c9a84c] text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase mb-2 font-display">Faction Guide</p>
          <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">Drukhari</h1>
          <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
            Raiders from the shadows. The Dark Eldar haunt the hidden city of Commorragh, 
            feeding their immortal souls on the suffering of others. The fastest army in 40k — 
            and the most dangerous glass cannon.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Quick stats -->
      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Playstyle</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">Glass Cannon Raiders</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Painting</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-yellow-400">Medium</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Rules</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-red-400">Hard</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Starter Cost</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">~$160</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mt-3 italic">*The Combat Patrol is Haemonculus Covens — tankier and slower than the classic raider playstyle. More on that below.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Lore -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">Who are the Drukhari?</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg">
        <p>
          Ten thousand years ago, the Eldar empire fell. Their hedonistic excesses across millennia 
          birthed a Chaos god — Slaanesh, the Prince of Pleasure — who devoured their souls 
          in an event called the Fall. The Craftworld Eldar survived by isolating themselves 
          on vast ark-ships. The Harlequins survived through devotion to the Laughing God. 
          The Drukhari survived by leaning in.
        </p>
        <p>
          They retreated into Commorragh, a hidden city tucked within the Webway — the ancient 
          pocket dimension that runs between realspace and the warp. There, shielded from 
          Slaanesh's reach, they found a solution to their problem: if you feel pain and suffering 
          acutely enough, it feeds your soul and wards off the god's hunger. So they raid. Constantly. 
          They descend on worlds without warning, take slaves, and return to Commorragh to conduct 
          their awful work on them.
        </p>
        <p>
          This isn't cruelty for cruelty's sake — it's survival. A Drukhari who doesn't feed 
          begins to wither, to age, to feel Slaanesh pulling at their soul. The suffering of 
          others is literally keeping them alive. This makes them some of the most nuanced 
          villains in 40k: completely monstrous, entirely understandable.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Playstyle -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">How they play on the table</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg mb-10">
        <p>
          Traditional Drukhari (Kabals and Wych Cults) are the <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">fastest army in Warhammer 40k</strong>. 
          Raiders — open-topped skimmer vehicles that move 14" — carry Kabalite Warriors who 
          disembark, unload a devastating volley of dark lance fire and poisoned splinter shots, 
          then fall back into the Raider and zoom out of charge range. Strike, retreat, repeat.
        </p>
        <p>
          The cost: almost nothing survives a return volley. Drukhari infantry are fragile. 
          Raiders are lightly armored. If your opponent catches you, you die. Playing Drukhari 
          well means never getting caught — using superior speed and positioning to always 
          have the angle, always have the escape route. It rewards players who enjoy chess-like 
          positioning puzzles.
        </p>
        <p>
          The <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Combat Patrol (Covens)</strong> plays differently: 
          slower, tankier, with monstrous Talos Pain Engines doing the heavy lifting. 
          Still Drukhari in flavor — still body horror and darkness — but the mobility 
          game is less extreme. A good entry point if you want to learn the faction 
          before investing in Raiders.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-green-400">Drukhari are for you if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✓ You love speed and positioning games</li>
            <li>✓ You want the most mobile army in 40k</li>
            <li>✓ You enjoy outwitting opponents through mobility</li>
            <li>✓ You're drawn to dark, alien aesthetics</li>
            <li>✓ Body horror and surgical horror appeal to you</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-red-400">Maybe look elsewhere if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✗ You want a forgiving, durable army</li>
            <li>✗ You're still learning the basics — Drukhari punish mistakes</li>
            <li>✗ You want a simple game plan</li>
            <li>✗ You hate assembling thin, detailed models</li>
            <li>✗ You want lots of shooting with no risk of dying</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Sub-factions -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">The three sub-factions</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-8 text-lg">
        Drukhari armies can mix sub-factions, but each has a distinct identity and playstyle. 
        The Combat Patrol is Covens. The classic raider experience is Kabals.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        {[
          {
            name: 'Kabals',
            tag: 'Noble raider houses',
            color: 'text-purple-400',
            desc: 'The aristocratic houses of Commorragh. Kabalite Warriors ride Raiders and Venoms — fast, open-topped vehicles — shooting poisoned splinters and dark lances, then retreating to safety. This is the classic Drukhari experience: high speed, glass cannon. The Archon is your commander.',
            models: 'Kabalite Warriors, Raiders, Ravagers, Archon',
          },
          {
            name: 'Wych Cults',
            tag: 'Arena gladiators',
            color: 'text-red-400',
            desc: 'Gladiatorial fighters who perform death-sports in Commorragh\'s arenas and bring that murderous skill to the battlefield. Wyches are exceptional in melee, dodging in combat and making enemy attacks less effective. Fast, melee-focused, and extremely fragile. For players who love high-risk close combat.',
            models: 'Wyches, Reavers, Hellions, Succubus',
          },
          {
            name: 'Haemonculus Covens',
            tag: 'Mad scientist body horror (Combat Patrol)',
            color: 'text-green-400',
            desc: 'The flesh-crafters of Commorragh. Haemonculi are centuries-old surgeons who modify their own bodies and those of their Wracks into something inhuman. Slower than the other sub-factions but significantly tougher. Talos Pain Engines are monstrous creatures that regenerate wounds. A more forgiving entry into Drukhari.',
            models: 'Haemonculus, Wracks, Talos, Cronos',
          },
        ].map(sub => (
          <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
            <div class="flex items-center flex-wrap gap-3 mb-2">
              <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-lg">{sub.name}</h3>
              <span class={`text-xs font-semibold ${sub.color}`}>{sub.tag}</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">{sub.desc}</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">Key models: {sub.models}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="mt-6 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-5">
        <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Important:</strong> If the fast raider playstyle appeals to you more than Covens, 
          consider skipping the Combat Patrol and starting with a 
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Kabalite Warriors box + Raider</strong> instead. 
          It's cheaper, and you'll be learning the army's actual identity from turn one.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Painting -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">How to paint Drukhari</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-8 text-lg">
        Using the Combat Patrol (Covens) as the example — dark purple armor with exposed 
        flesh tones, surgical tubes, and bone details. Grim, distinctive, and more forgiving 
        to paint than it looks.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4 mb-10">
        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">1</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Prime black, base coat the armor Naggaroth Night</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Chaos Black spray, then Naggaroth Night (dark purple) over all armor panels. The deep purple is the Drukhari identity — dark enough to look almost black, but clearly purple in good light.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">2</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Shade with Druchii Violet</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Apply Druchii Violet shade over all the armor. It deepens the purple and creates shadows in the panel lines. Let it dry fully before the next step.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">3</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Layer the raised panels Xereus Purple</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Apply Xereus Purple to the raised armor edges and surfaces, leaving the recesses dark. Then edge highlight with Genestealer Purple (or Daemonette Hide) on the sharpest corners. This creates the sleek Drukhari look.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">4</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Paint exposed flesh (Wracks, Haemonculus)</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Kislev Flesh as the base coat over all exposed skin and muscle. Apply Reikland Fleshshade into the recesses. Then highlight back up with Kislev Flesh. For tubes and veins: a thin line of Cadian Fleshtone.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">5</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Bone and surgical details</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Ushabti Bone on rib cages, bone protrusions, and equipment. Shade with Agrax Earthshade. Drybrush Screaming Skull on top. Metallic blades: Leadbelcher → Nuln Oil → edge with Stormhost Silver.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">6</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Eyes and gemstones</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Eyes: Mephiston Red base, Blood Angel Red Contrast or Carroburg Crimson shade, small dot of white for a gleam. Gemstones on armor: Moot Green or Caledor Sky base with a white highlight dot. Done.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-5">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-2">The Contrast paint shortcut</h3>
        <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Prime <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Chaos Black</strong> → apply 
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Shyish Purple Contrast</strong> over armor → 
          apply <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Guilliman Flesh Contrast</strong> over skin and tubes → 
          pick out metals in Leadbelcher. The Contrast paints shade themselves over black. 
          Not the showroom finish, but Drukhari that look unmistakably Drukhari on a game table.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- What to buy -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">What to buy first</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-10 text-lg">Start with the Combat Patrol for the most cost-effective entry — but read the sub-faction note above if raiders are calling to you.</p>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-4">
          <span class="bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-display mr-2">Start Here</span>
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$160</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Combat Patrol: Drukhari</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          Includes a Haemonculus (one of 40k's most character-rich models), a Cronos, 
          a Talos Pain Engine, and 10 Wracks — 13 models total. 
          A Haemonculus Covens force: tough, monstrous, and deeply weird. 
          The Haemonculus alone is worth the box for hobbyists.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FS2J7JDV?tag=grimdarkprime-20"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Search Amazon →
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-3">
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$80 · alternative raider start</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Kabalite Warriors + Raider (if you want raiders)</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          If the fast glass-cannon playstyle is why you chose Drukhari, start here instead. 
          A Raider full of Kabalite Warriors is the core unit of a Kabal army. 
          Learn the movement game from turn one rather than adapting later.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=kabalite+warriors+raider+drukhari+warhammer+40k&tag=grimdarkprime-20"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Search Amazon →
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Paints -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-4">Paints you need (Covens scheme)</h3>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          {[
            { name: 'Chaos Black Spray', use: 'Primer', required: true },
            { name: 'Naggaroth Night', use: 'Dark purple armor base coat', required: true },
            { name: 'Druchii Violet', use: 'Shade wash — armor depth', required: true },
            { name: 'Xereus Purple', use: 'Layer — raised armor panels', required: true },
            { name: 'Kislev Flesh', use: 'Exposed flesh, tubes, and skin', required: true },
            { name: 'Reikland Fleshshade', use: 'Shade for flesh areas', required: true },
            { name: 'Ushabti Bone', use: 'Bone protrusions and rib cages', required: true },
            { name: 'Leadbelcher', use: 'Metallic blades and tools', required: false },
            { name: 'Genestealer Purple', use: 'Edge highlights on armor corners', required: false },
          ].map(paint => (
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class={`text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 font-display ${paint.required ? 'bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113]' : 'border border-[#2a2a35] text-[#4a4855]'}`}>
                {paint.required ? 'Essential' : 'Optional'}
              </span>
              <div>
                <span class="text-sm font-semibold">{paint.name}</span>
                <span class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm"> — {paint.use}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Cost breakdown -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-8">Honest cost breakdown</h2>
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
        {[
          { item: 'Combat Patrol: Drukhari', cost: '~$160', note: '13 models — playable Covens force' },
          { item: 'Essential paints (7)', cost: '~$42', note: 'Purple armor + flesh tones + bone' },
          { item: 'Basing supplies', cost: '~$12', note: 'Texture paint + tufts' },
          { item: 'Clippers + hobby knife', cost: '~$20', note: 'One-time purchase' },
          { item: 'Superglue + plastic glue', cost: '~$10', note: 'These models need both for fine parts' },
        ].map((row, i) => (
          <div class={`flex items-start justify-between px-5 py-4 gap-4 ${i % 2 === 0 ? '' : 'bg-[#111113]'}`}>
            <div>
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold">{row.item}</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mt-0.5">{row.note}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] flex-shrink-0">{row.cost}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-4 bg-[#1f1d14] border-t border-[#c9a84c]">
          <p class="font-display font-semibold">All-in starter total</p>
          <span class="font-display font-bold text-[#c9a84c] text-lg">~$244</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">
        Drukhari models are among the most detailed in 40k — assembly takes patience. 
        Raider skimmers have many fine parts. Take your time with assembly; it pays off in the final model.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="px-6 py-20 text-center">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold mb-4">From the Webway, they come.</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg mb-8">
        Pain is currency. Suffering is life. Choose your sub-faction, 
        grab the Combat Patrol or a Raider, and learn to move faster than your opponent can react.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
        <a
          href="/painting"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display tracking-wide"
        >
          Painting Guide →
        </a>
        <a
          href="/quiz"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Retake the Quiz
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
